  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 石\ntitle: stone\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-1, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 石\nradicalNumber: 112\nonyomi: [セキ, シャク, コク]\nkunyomi: [いし]\ndistractors: [右, 口, 古]\n---\n\n# 石 — stone\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 石 (no. 112) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n[石](../words/石.md) いし names a stone or rock.\nThe character remains useful in compounds for precious stones and petroleum, though those words need their own translations.\nHere 石 is both the complete character and its indexing radical.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the lower box as a stone under a sloping ledge.\nThat image uses the present shape; it is not offered as the character's original drawing.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| いし | kun | [石](../words/石.md) いし — stone |\n| セキ | on | 石油 せきゆ — petroleum; 宝石 ほうせき — precious stone |\n\nシャク and コク are also retained in metadata; this table concentrates on the examples below.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [石](../words/石.md) いし — stone; pebble\n- 石油 せきゆ — petroleum\n- 宝石 ほうせき — gem; precious stone\n\n## Notes\n\n道に小さな石があります。 (みちにちいさないしがあります。) — There is a small stone on the road.\n\n[右](右.md) is especially close in shape: watch the upper strokes and their crossing.\n[口](口.md) lacks the top entirely; [古](古.md) has 十 above the box rather than 石's slanting stroke.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nWords: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1382440, 1382830, 1516220.\n",
